<sn><md>### Basic Command Structure

```bash
rclone COMMAND LOCAL_PATH REMOTE:PATH
```

For example:

```bash
rclone copy ~/Documents mega:Backup
```

Here:

```text
~/Documents ─────────────► mega:Backup
     SOURCE                DESTINATION
   💻 Local                  ☁️ Cloud
```


**Using `copy`**

```text
💻 LOCAL                         ☁️ CLOUD

📁 Documents                     📁 Backup
├── 📄 A.txt ──────────────────► 📄 A.txt
├── 📄 B.txt ──────────────────► 📄 B.txt
└── 📄 C.txt ──────────────────► 📄 C.txt

Local files: ✔️ Remain
Cloud files: ✔️ Copied
```

Command:

```bash
rclone copy ~/Documents mega:Backup
```

Extra files already in the cloud are **not deleted**.

</md></sn><sn><md>### Using `move`

```text
💻 LOCAL                         ☁️ CLOUD

📁 Documents                     📁 Backup

📄 A.txt ──────────────────────► 📄 A.txt
📄 B.txt ──────────────────────► 📄 B.txt
📄 C.txt ──────────────────────► 📄 C.txt


After successful transfer:

💻 LOCAL                         ☁️ CLOUD

📁 Documents                     📁 Backup
                                ├── 📄 A.txt
                                ├── 📄 B.txt
                                └── 📄 C.txt
```

Command:

```bash
rclone move ~/Documents mega:Backup
```

The local files are removed after successful transfer.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Using `sync`

```text
💻 LOCAL                         ☁️ CLOUD

📁 Documents                     📁 Backup
├── 📄 A.txt ──────────────────► 📄 A.txt
├── 📄 B.txt ──────────────────► 📄 B.txt
└── 📄 C.txt ──────────────────► 📄 C.txt
                                 ❌ Old.txt
```

After synchronization:

```text
💻 LOCAL                         ☁️ CLOUD

📁 Documents                     📁 Backup
├── 📄 A.txt                     ├── 📄 A.txt
├── 📄 B.txt                     ├── 📄 B.txt
└── 📄 C.txt                     └── 📄 C.txt
```

Command:

```bash
rclone sync ~/Documents mega:Backup
```

`sync` makes the cloud destination identical to the local source. Therefore, files existing only in the cloud can be deleted.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Summary

| Operation | Direction | Source Files             | Extra Cloud Files |
| --------- | --------- | ------------------------ | ----------------- |
| `copy`    | 💻 → ☁️   | ✔️ Remain                | ✔️ Remain         |
| `move`    | 💻 → ☁️   | ❌ Removed after transfer | ✔️ Remain         |
| `sync`    | 💻 → ☁️   | ✔️ Remain                | ❌ Deleted         |

&gt; ⚠️ Always use `--dry-run` before running an important synchronization:

```bash
rclone sync ~/Documents mega:Backup --dry-run
```
</md></sn>